{
  "title": "mcu",
  "summary": "U1 is a Seeed XIAO nRF52840, soldered by its castellated edge pads; the only underside pad used is VBAT (solder through a plated hole from the back). SPI to the ADS131M08 is on the XIAO's default SPI pins D8/D9/D10 with 33 ohm series resistors to slow the edges near the analog front end. D7 = CS, D6 = DRDY (interrupt), D5 = SYNC/RESET (pulled up so the ADC is not held in reset while the XIAO boots), D4 = ANA_EN for the analog LDO. The ADC master clock defaults to 8 MHz from D3 through R5; Y1 (8.192 MHz oscillator) with R6 and C1 is an unfitted alternative: fit Y1, C1, R6 and remove R5 to switch. D0-D2 (analog-capable) are spare. VBUS sensing needs no pin: VBUS reaches the nRF inside the module. FIRMWARE NOTE: when ANA_EN is low the ADC is unpowered, so drive every ADC-facing pin low or high-Z first, or the ADC back-powers through its input diodes.",
